// The other hostages at Noviodunum: children of other peoples.
=== start
[flag epo_out] -> after
They look at you, decide you're nobody's father, and answer anyway, in Gallic with a Latin word in every sentence.
* "Where are you from?" -> where
* "Do you want to go home?" -> home
* "Goodbye." -> END

=== where
"Lingones." Or "Senones," or "Treveri," or a people you've never heard of from somewhere near the sea. "My father is a chief. He sent me." A pause. "He sent me so they wouldn't burn our village. So I'm worth a village." It's said with pride, and something under the pride.
-> END

=== home
They look at you as if you've asked whether they'd like to fly. "When the war ends. If my people keep faith." A shrug, learned from the older ones. "If they don't, they sell us. Orbius told us. He tells us everything. He says it's kinder."
-> END

=== after
"Is it true?" A small voice. "Eponina's gone home? Orbius wrote her dead, but she isn't, is she?" They look at you very hard. "We won't tell."
-> END
